{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For a US-listed equity ETF, separate **one-time launch costs**—legal formation and registration, listing, index licensing or methodology, platform onboarding, connectivity, and distribution setup—from seed capital. Seed capital is fund assets, not an expense; it supports trading, remains exposed to market risk, and may be redeemed.\n\nRecurring costs include management, administration, accounting, custody, transfer agency, index and listing fees, regulatory costs, audit, tax, legal/compliance, reporting, and service providers. Under a unitary fee, the sponsor typically covers specified operating expenses; contracts should define exclusions, often brokerage, financing, taxes, and extraordinary items. Fund trading costs and portfolio taxes reduce NAV; investors bear bid–ask spreads and their own platform charges.\n\nFor each item, model payer, timing, basis, and exclusions; quotes vary. Break-even occurs when fee revenue (rate × average net assets) covers sponsor-borne costs. Retained margin requires revenue above those costs, accounting for asset variability and waivers."}}
